<%--
Default_Attributes_Follow_Prototype_Chain - <Define> default attributes resolve through
exactly the chain templates do.

Audit bug 21: _apply_default_attributes() walked only the `extends=` chain, so a slot-only
JS subclass got its parent's TEMPLATE but none of the parent <Define>'s class/attrs.
Audit LOW (component.ts ~:2170): `if (!this.$.attr(key))` treated "0" and "" as unset, so
an invocation tabindex="0" was overwritten by the Define's tabindex="-1".
--%>
<Define:Default_Attributes_Follow_Prototype_Chain>
  <div>
    <h1>Define defaults follow the prototype chain</h1>
    <Da_Child $sid="child" />
    <Da_Base $sid="zero" tabindex="0" />
    <Da_Base $sid="empty" title="" />
    <div $sid="stage"></div>
  </div>
</Define:Default_Attributes_Follow_Prototype_Chain>
